## Research Summary

I have analyzed the newly launched AI coding tools from the last 14 days (May 11-15, 2026) and found **14 products** that meet the criteria of being AI coding/developer tools. All products have been verified for launch dates and relevance to the AI development workflow space.

### Key Findings by Category:

**AI IDE (1 product):**
- **Warp** - Open-source agentic development environment with AI-first architecture

**Code Agents & Orchestration (7 products):**
- **Stagent** - Workflow orchestrator for Claude Code
- **RoBrain** - Shared AI memory system for teams
- **Weavable** - Persistent work context infrastructure
- **Open Computer Use** - Computer-use agent framework
- **Open Browser Use** - Browser automation framework
- **Asteroid** - Rapid AI agent builder
- **Comie.dev** - Production context layer for AI agents

**AI Coding CLI/Tools (2 products):**
- **Claudy** - Multi-session Claude Code workspace manager
- **Agent FM** - File manager for Claude Code & Codex

**Workflow-Specific Tools (2 products):**
- **Graphbit PRFlow** - AI-powered code reviewer
- **Latitude** - Claude Code observability tool

**Infrastructure/Platform (2 products):**
- **display.dev** - Deployment platform for AI-generated content
- **Openclaw OS** - AI app development platform

**Developer Tools (1 product):**
- **Raindrop Workshop** - Local debugger for AI agents

The products have been sorted by relevance (prioritizing direct AI coding agents, IDEs, and workflow tools) and recency, with the final result saved to `new-product.json`.

